<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26374" root="طبن" body-key="T">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طِبْنٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طُبْنَةٌ</span>: ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  and see also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَبْنٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الطِّبْنُ</span>
also signifies <i>What the wind brings,</i> [or <i>bears
along,</i>] <i>of firewood</i> [app. meaning of fragments
thereof], and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">النَّمَش</span>: [but this seems to be a
mistranscription; for it is immediately added,]
and sometimes <i>the house</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">البيت</span>) <i>that is built,</i> or
<i>constructed, therewith</i> is thus called. (TA.)

  </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
